<title>FRANCE: LVMH has no comment on GrandMet remarks.</title>
<headline>LVMH has no comment on GrandMet remarks.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton declined on Thursday to comment on remarks by Grand Metropolitan's chief executive that a three-way drinks deal could be reached this year if benefits are fairly shared.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for the French group said LVMH was waiting for a reply from Guinness and GrandMet on chairman Bernard Arnault's proposal to create an independent, listed company blending the three companies' wine and spirits businesses.</p>
<p>&quot;We are waiting for the final answer from Guinness and GrandMet,&quot; the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>GrandMet chief executive John McGrath was quoted in the Financial Times as saying that any new deal &quot;must demonstrate&quot; that Guinness and GrandMet shareholders would benefit.</p>
</text>
